<details>
  <summary>Data sources &amp; methodology</summary>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>CPU scores</strong> — Geekbench 6 averages from <a href="https://browser.geekbench.com/mac-benchmarks">browser.geekbench.com</a> (Mac) and <a href="https://browser.geekbench.com/ios-benchmarks">iOS benchmarks</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>GPU Raster</strong> — Geekbench 6 Metal compute score.</li>
    <li><strong>GPU RT</strong> — Relative score. M3 and A17 Pro are the baselines (100). Earlier chips lacked hardware ray tracing. Gains based on Apple's published claims and independent benchmarks.</li>
    <li><strong>Power Efficiency</strong> — Single-core score divided by estimated sustained power draw. 15 W for M-series (fanless MacBook Air), 5 W for A-series (iPhone).</li>
    <li><strong>Die Size</strong> — Published die area in mm² from teardown reports and Apple disclosures. M5 is estimated.</li>
    <li><strong>Neural Engine</strong> — Peak TOPS as published by Apple.</li>
  </ul>
</details>

